<title>UK: El Al says 3 sting-rays born in flight from Miami.</title>
<headline>El Al says 3 sting-rays born in flight from Miami.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>El Al Israel Airlines said on Wednesday that three baby sting-rays now on display at the recently opened London Aquarium were spawned in mid-air in ideal conditions.</p>
<p>&quot;We recently flew in from Miami to London two stingrays plus four brown and three sand tiger sharks, along with tropical fish, on a Boeing 747 cargo flight,&quot; said El Al spokesman Lee Silverman.</p>
<p>&quot;We have been told one of the stingrays gave birth to three babies, which we believe happened during the flight in a container with a specially-controlled oxygen level,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Silverman said the in-flight cargo conditions were &quot;ideal for the birth&quot;.</p>
<p>The rays, sharks and tropical fish were caught in the Florida keys.</p>
<p>--Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel +44 171 542 7076; fax +5017 -www.racs.com</p>
